      "message": "fix(verify): judge a stock-sourced Bore's entry rapid against the stock\n\nThe planar ladder rapids to the top of the cut plus the plunge height;\nfor Bore that top is the hole's mouth. Under a block standing higher\nthan the mouth the rapid ends in uncut stock. Pocket, Contour and a\npart-sourced Bore were already convicted by the rapid law (#96), but a\nBore whose source is the stock posted silently: the column law read\n\"is this stock?\" from the op's region, which for Bore and Thread is\nthe stock footprint with the holes' rims punched out.\n\nmaterial_source::judged_stock hands the verify (upright and 3+2) the\nstock's own facets for a stock-sourced Bore or Thread; every other\nsource and kind reads as before. Pinned by ladder_entry_height.rs over\nPocket, Bore and Contour: convicted and blocked 5 mm under the block,\nsilent inside the plunge height and with stock to the mouth, acquitted\nby a face ahead.\n\nFixes #1066\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
